Logic :

The problem is to find the minimum path sum from the top of a triangle to the bottom. From each element, I can move to either the element directly below it or the element below-right.

I use bottom-up dynamic programming. Starting from the second-last row, for every element I choose the minimum of its two children and add that value to the current element. This gives the minimum path sum from that position to the bottom.

I update the triangle in-place, so I don't need a separate DP array. After processing all rows, the top element contains the minimum path sum

Code :

class Solution {
    public int minimumTotal(List<List<Integer>> triangle) {
        int size=triangle.size();
        for(int i=size-2;i>=0;i--){
            for(int j=0;j<triangle.get(i).size();j++){
                triangle.get(i).set(j,triangle.get(i).get(j)+Math.min(triangle.get(i+1).get(j),triangle.get(i+1).get(j+1)));
            }
        }
        return triangle.get(0).get(0);
    }
}
